rom extreme emotional  distress eventually the creature will be  unable to take it anymore standing up  scp-096 will then travel towards whoever  dared to look at it using anomalous  speed to hunt down the person that saw  its face the foundation has proven that  it is unquestionably impossible for  anyone to hide from scp-096  literally nothing can stand in its path  as it tracks down its victim not walls  or locked doors even being aboard a boat  in the middle of the ocean or in a plane  in mid-air can prevent it from finding  you and when it does find you it's not a  pleasant sight  scp-096 will kill the person that looked  at it without leaving any detectable  trace on their body the monster is  impervious to gunfire and all other  forms of conventional weaponry it can't  be killed or even so much as harmed even  if the shy guy is only seen as a tiny  little speck in a photograph this will  be enough to trigger the creature's  relentless defense mechanism so because  of this the scp foundation's only real  way to keep the creature safely locked  up is in an airtight steel cube with no  security cameras or surveillance tools  of any kind all members of personnel are  reminded that they are to never ever  look at it but what if they could what  if somehow someone was able to  neutralize  scp-096's anomalous abilities or was  resistant to being killed when the  creature inevitably tracked them down  this is how the tale known as picture  perfect begins what do you think boys is  she a beauty or what dr kleff proclaimed  to a group of his fellow high-ranking  foundation researchers the group looked  in confusion and unease at what clef had  been referring to namely a photograph  that he just hung up on the wall of his  office a photo of what though well a  four foot by five foot picture of none  other than  scp-096 of course naturally the other  researchers shared a mixture of shock  and dismay at what clef had just done as  you would if one of your co-workers hung  up a photo of a creature that could kill  you just for looking at that said photo  we've lost a number of staff members  from around the scp-explained office  that same way let's just say the  christmas party last year was not that  fun dr klaff had long been one of the  more enigmatic and mysterious scientists  working at the foundation with the  exception of the elusive and infamous o5  council alto clef was formerly an  operative for the global occult  coalition as well as being known to be a  bit of a gun enthusiast and all-around  crazy wild card clef earned his own  brand of infamy for his rumored practice  of brutally decommissioning dangerous  scps and you can probably guess what we  mean by that he's the foundation's go-to  executioner and a specialist in dealing  with reality bending anomalies would you  expect any less from an ex-goc joining  clef in his office were the likes of dr  jack bright another infamous foundation  researcher dr bright also known as  scp-963-2 was assigned to conduct  experiments on an anomalous amulet as cp  963 which resulted in his death at the  hands of scp-076  abel however anomalous properties of the  amulet gave bright the ability to  inhabit new bodies after his death  specifically anyone who also touches the  amulet which kills the host and allows  bright to take control of their body  while technically immortal dr bright  isn't exactly stoked about that fact  often seeking out death and wanting to  know exactly what it feels like also  present at the unveiling of dr cliff's  photo of scp-096 was his friendly rival  dr kondraki while usually gruff and  antisocial kondraki is an expert in  perception based anomalies normally  called upon by the foundation to  photograph scps that would otherwise be  invisible or imperceivable dr sumerian a  member of the foundation's ethics  committee was also in the room as dr  cleff proudly showed off his office's  latest decoration perhaps the most  outwardly strange researcher in  attendance was kane pathos crow a  scientist from the foundation's research  department who had been transformed into  a labrador retriever after an experiment  that needless to say went a bit awry  crow must have been barking up the wrong  tree on that one each of them expressed  their reactions differently deeply  exasperated dr sumerian shook his head  and began to question his recent  decision to stop drinking meanwhile dr  bright looked up at the painting with a  bemused tilting of his head he wondered  if scp-096 would come to kill him and if  it did would it only do so once or would  the creature try again and again each  time that bright inhabited a new body  perhaps in an attempt to look away from  the photo kane lowered his head and  covered his snout with a paw while dr  kondraki hung his head in deep  disappointment the only one among the  group that seemed unaffected by the  sight of the scp-096 photograph was dr  charles gears another high-ranking scp  foundation scientist it was gears who  finally broke the uncomfortable silence  asking dr cleff the one question that  had been on everyone's minds  why clef excitedly exclaimed that the  photo was meant to be in celebration of  scp-096 finally having been neutralized  and according to the scientists they  were free to look the creature's ugly  mug all they wanted the group stared in  horror at the gaping mouth the screaming  expression of the monster that had  killed so many people not one of them  shared in dr cleff's enthusiasm some  like bright and gear simply argued that  the picture was creepy while others  voiced far greater concerns kane argued  that putting up a photo of scp-096 was  in poor taste that it was massively  disrespectful to all the unwitting  victims that the shy guy had killed over  the years it was also reckless and  dangerous dr sumerian added it had not  yet been a full 24 hours since  scp-096's apparent death and if the  creature was somehow able to come back  to life it could kill every researcher  in the office by showing them this  so-called masterpiece clef had put all  of his co-workers lives at risk he  showed off their concerns of the  creature coming back to life despite  knowing that this was entirely possible  after all it wasn't just anomalies and  scps that could defy death most of the  foundation's higher ranking staff were  also capable of the same even some of  the researchers in that very room had  died at least once dr kleff claimed that  should the worst happen in scp-096  return to life they could simply forget  its face with amnestics clef claimed  that they were now free of  scp-096's anomalous powers thanks to the  creature's termination but the four men  and one dog in his office with him  failed to share his enthusiasm the group  then began debating why the foundation  even needed to neutralize scp-096 in the  first place with its containment purely  hinged on nobody ever looking at the  creature he could be contained by  putting a sack over his head dr bright  pointed out met with murmurs of  agreement from the others that's where  you're wrong jack there could be photos  of him from before he was contained or  someone could get a hold of the photos  we already have of him dr cliff argued  back if they did something like hack  markiplier's youtube account put that  photo on the homepage it'd be game over  the shy guy would breach containment  with millions of dash ones to kill all  over the world and that kind of rampage  would guarantee he'd have cameras  pointed on him 24 7. exposure would grow  exponentially until the bastard  slaughtered most of the civilization as  far as i'm concerned he should have been  classified as ketter from the star but  bright argued back stating that the  foundation had no real cause to kill  scp-096  they already had a clear understanding  that the shy guy's anomalous behaviors  were only even triggered by somebody  observing it and preventing that from  happening was pretty easy killing the  creature just seemed excessive cruel  even sumerian chimed in again saying  that killing scp-096 was something the  global occult coalition would do and the  foundation still hadn't learned all they  could about zero nine six could someone  survive looking at the creature if they  were in space or another dimension now  no one would ever know on top of that dr  gears pointed out that the foundation  had no clue what  scp-096's exact origin was where the  creature had come from if it was the  only one of its kind or whether it was a  part of a species of similar monsters if  more beings like the shy guy could exist  in the future they could cause a global  catastrophe but despite all the points  raised by his colleagues dr cleff didn't  want to hear any of what they had to say  all right i hear what you're all saying  but shut up the shy guy was a sword of  damocles dangling over the whole world  we killed him and we're gonna celebrate  that by doing the one thing we could  never do while he was alive looking at  his face each and every day for the rest  of our lives so that we never forget  what we've won and could have lost the  four researchers and the one who had  been turned into a dog all took a moment  to consider clef's argument more  courtesy than he had extended to them  they all looked up at the haunting  grotesque face of scp-096 once more as  much as they protested the decision to  have the creature killed each of them  secretly hoped it stayed neutralized  especially now that clef was using  scp-096's photo as an office decoration  if the creature ever managed to come  back anyone that set foot in cleft's  office and looked at the picture was as  good as dead finally dr kondraki spoke  up and threatened to resign cleft to one  of the worst positions imaginable  critiquing first drafts of scp reports  by junior researchers for a moment clef  thought his rival was bluffing but  eventually decided it was better to be  safe than sorry as the gunhow foundation  scientist begrudgingly pulled the photo  from his office wall he muttered to the  group none of you appreciate post-modern  art now go check out scp-096 shy guy  escape incident  096-1-8 containment breach at scp-096  look at a picture of shy guy in space  the shy guy questions and theories for  more on the legendary shy guy

